value_loss": 0.0}]}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N5\nN11 -> terminal\nN4 -> N8\nN1 -> N9, N8\nN10 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN3 -> N6\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> N3, N0\nN7 -> N11\nN9 -> N7, N11\nN5 -> N10, N1, N4\n\nLegal moves: N3, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N3 or N0.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to N6, which ends in terminal (win for opponent if it's their turn).  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N5, from which the opponent can go to N10 (terminal) or N1 or N4.  \n  - N1 leads to N9 or N8; N9 leads to N7 or N11 (both terminal), N8 is terminal.  \n  - N4 leads to N8 (terminal).  \n  - N5 → N10 (terminal) is a winning move for the player who reaches it.  \nThus, from N5, the opponent can immediately win by going to N10.  \nSo from N2, going to N0 allows opponent to win immediately via N5 → N10.  \nGoing to N3: N3 → N6 → terminal. So the current player wins immediately.  \nThus, choosing N3 wins the game.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": -1.0, "llm_raw_text": "<|im_start|>assistant\n<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N3 or N0.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to N6, which ends in terminal (win for opponent if it's their turn).  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N5, from which the opponent can go to N10 (terminal) or N1 or N4.  \n  - N1 leads to N9 or N8; N9 leads to N7 or N11 (both terminal), N8 is terminal.  \n  - N4 leads to N8 (terminal).  \n  - N5 → N10 (terminal) is a winning move for the player who reaches it.  \nThus, from N5, the opponent can immediately win by going to N10.  \nSo from N2, going to N0 allows opponent to win immediately via N5 → N10.  \nGoing to N3: N3 → N6 → terminal. So the current player wins immediately.  \nThus, choosing N3 wins the game.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer><|im_end|>", "tag": "Geography-Val-D3-IID", "minimax_decision_records": [{"turn_index": 0, "player_id": 0, "action": "N3", "valid": 1.0, "format_valid": 1.0, "semantic_action_valid": 1.0, "action_recovered": 0.0, "near_generation_limit": 0.0, "response_truncated": 0.0, "graph_id": "a8b5775f24909de6", "graph_seed": "5570916710260285388088", "graph_current_node": "N2", "graph_node_count": 12, "graph_transposition_rate": 0.18181818181818182, "remaining_optimal_distance": 3, "current_out_degree": 2, "spread": 2.0, "regret": 1.0, "optimal": 0.0, "counterfactual_baseline": 0.0, "counterfactual_advantage": -1.0, "value_loss": 2.0}]}]

