tes.  \nThus, moving to N0 leads to immediate terminal state for opponent. So N0 is a winning move. Among all options, N0 is the safest and guarantees a win. Therefore, choosing N0 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>From N2, the legal moves are to N8, N0, or N6. We analyze each destination to determine which leads to a winning position (i.e., forces the opponent into a losing position).  \n- N8 → N0 or N6: N0 → N7 (terminal), N6 → N1 or N3. N1 and N7 are terminal, so if N6 leads to N1 or N3, those are terminal. N3 → N9 → N4 (terminal), so all paths from N6 eventually end.  \n- N0 → N7 (terminal), so the opponent loses immediately.  \n- N6 → N1 or N3: both lead to terminal states.  \nThus, moving to N0 leads to immediate terminal state for opponent. So N0 is a winning move. Among all options, N0 is the safest and guarantees a win. Therefore, choosing N0 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}]
