g to N0 leads to N9 (terminal), so the opponent has no move and wins immediately. Moving to N4 leads to N3 or N5. N5 leads to N2 or N1 (both terminal), so opponent loses. N3 leads to N1 or N7 (both terminal), so opponent loses. Thus, moving to N4 ensures the opponent faces a terminal node on their turn, meaning we win. Therefore, N4 is the optimal move.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}]
