": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the player can move to N9 or N4. Moving to N4 leads to N5 or N7. From N5, the player can go to N6 (terminal) or N3 (terminal), both of which end the game immediately. From N7, the player can go to N8 (terminal) or N9. N9 leads back to N6 or N0, and N0 leads to N2 (terminal). This creates a cycle with potential for infinite play, but since the game ends when a player cannot move, and all paths eventually reach terminal nodes, we must evaluate which move forces the opponent into a losing position. Moving to N9 immediately gives the opponent a choice: N6 (terminal) or N0 (to N2, terminal). Either way, the opponent loses immediately. Thus, moving to N9 is optimal as it forces the opponent into a terminal move. Therefore, the best first move is to N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}]
