[2026-08-13 21:03:03] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 228008] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN1 -> N5\nN2 -> N6, N3\nN0 -> N5, N1\nN7 -> N4, N2\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN4 -> N0, N8\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> N9, N0\n\nLegal moves: N4, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N4 or N2. Moving to N2 leads to N6 or N3. N3 goes to terminal (win for the player who moves there), and N6 goes to terminal. So N2 leads to a winning position for the next player. Moving to N4 leads to N0 or N8. N0 leads to N5 or N1; N5 and N1 both eventually lead to terminal. N8 leads to N9 or N0; N9 is terminal. Thus, all paths from N4 eventually reach terminal. However, from N2, the opponent is forced into a terminal node on their next move. Thus, moving to N2 gives the current player a winning strategy. Therefore, choosing N2 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N4 or N2. Moving to N2 leads to N6 or N3. N3 goes to terminal (win for the player who moves there), and N6 goes to terminal. So N2 leads to a winning position for the next player. Moving to N4 leads to N0 or N8. N0 leads to N5 or N1; N5 and N1 both eventually lead to terminal. N8 leads to N9 or N0; N9 is terminal. Thus, all paths from N4 eventually reach terminal. However, from N2, the opponent is forced into a terminal node on their next move. Thus, moving to N2 gives the current player a w