[2026-08-13 21:17:15] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 228008] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> N5, N3\nN8 -> N9, N0\nN2 -> N4, N6\nN6 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> N2, N7\nN3 -> N5\nN7 -> N2, N8\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N2, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the player can move to N2 or N7. Moving to N2 leads to N4 or N6. N6 goes directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately. N4 leads to N5 or N3; N5 and N3 both lead to terminal, so any move from N4 eventually ends in terminal. Similarly, N7 leads to N2 or N8; N8 leads to N9 or N0, both of which go to terminal. Thus, moving to N2 gives the first player a path to terminal via N6, which is a winning move. Moving to N7 leads to a cycle (N2 or N8), which may allow the opponent to force a win. Therefore, choosing N2 maximizes the chance of winning by immediately setting up a terminal path via N6.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the player can move to N2 or N7. Moving to N2 leads to N4 or N6. N6 goes directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately. N4 leads to N5 or N3; N5 and N3 both lead to terminal, so any move from N4 eventually ends in terminal. Similarly, N7 leads to N2 or N8; N8 leads to N9 or N0, both of which go to terminal. Thus, moving to N2 gives the first player a path to terminal via N6, which is a winning move. Moving to N7 leads to a cycle (N2 or N8), which may allow