n, but eventually leads to terminal states.  \n  - However, from N9 → N8 → N12 or N6 (both terminal), so opponent wins immediately.  \nThus, moving to N3 gives immediate win. N3 leads to terminal nodes directly, so the opponent has no move. Therefore, choosing N3 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N12, N6\nN1 -> N3, N9\nN13 -> N10, N11\nN0 -> terminal\nN10 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN11 -> N4, N5\nN6 -> terminal\nN3 -> N0, N7\nN9 -> N2, N8\nN12 -> terminal\nN2 -> N4, N13\nN5 -> N10, N0\n\nLegal moves: N0, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N0 or N7. Both N0 and N7 lead to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately, as the opponent has no legal move. Thus, either move ends the game on the first turn. Since both options result in an immediate win for the current player, either is optimal. Choosing N0 or N7 is equivalent. We select N0 as it appears earlier in the graph.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N0 or N7. Both N0 and N7 lead to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately, as the opponent has no legal move. Thus, either move ends the game on the first turn. Since both options result in an immediate win for the current player, either is optimal. Choosing N0 or N7 is equivalent. We select N0 as it appears earlier in the graph.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt":