N7 -> N2, N6\nN2 -> N3, N9\nN4 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N4, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N4 or N5. Both N4 and N5 lead directly to terminal nodes, meaning the player who moves to either wins immediately, and the opponent has no move. Thus, moving to N4 or N5 ends the game on the next turn, and the current player wins. Since both options result in an immediate win, either is optimal. Choosing N5 is arbitrary but valid; however, N4 and N5 are symmetric in outcome. The choice between them does not affect the outcome. Selecting N5 is sufficient.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N4 or N5. Both N4 and N5 lead directly to terminal nodes, meaning the player who moves to either wins immediately, and the opponent has no move. Thus, moving to N4 or N5 ends the game on the next turn, and the current player wins. Since both options result in an immediate win, either is optimal. Choosing N5 is arbitrary but valid; however, N4 and N5 are symmetric in outcome. The choice between them does not affect the outcome. Selecting N5 is sufficient.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}]
