aximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN3 -> N4, N1\nN0 -> N5, N9\nN6 -> N7, N5\nN4 -> N0, N6\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> N2\nN8 -> terminal\nN9 -> N6, N8\n\nLegal moves: N4, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N4 or N1.  \n- Moving to N1: N1 → N2 → terminal. Player who moves to N2 wins immediately. So the player who moves to N1 wins.  \n- Moving to N4: N4 → N0 or N6.  \n  - N0 → N5 or N9  \n    - N5 → terminal  \n    - N9 → N6 or N8  \n      - N6 → N7 or N5 (both lead to terminal)  \n      - N8 → terminal  \n  - So from N4, the game branches into paths that eventually reach terminal, but with alternating control.  \n  Since N1 leads directly to terminal in two moves (N3→N1→N2→terminal), the player who moves to N1 wins immediately.  \nThus, choosing N1 guarantees a win. N4 leads to a longer game with potential for the opponent to win. Therefore, N1 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N4 or N1.  \n- Moving to N1: N1 → N2 → terminal. Player who moves to N2 wins immediately. So the player who moves to N1 wins.  \n- Moving to N4: N4 → N0 or N6.  \n  - N0 → N5 or N9  \n    - N5 → terminal  \n    - N9 → N6 or N8  \n      - N6 → N7 or N5 (both lead to terminal)  \n      - N8 → terminal  \n  - So from N4, the game branches into paths that eventually reach terminal, but with alternating control.  \n  Since N1 leads directly to terminal in two moves (N3→N1→N2→terminal), the player who moves to N1 wins immediately.  \nThus, choosing N1 guarantees a win. N4 leads to a longer game with potential for the opponent to win. Therefore, N1 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"