[2026-08-13 21:31:02] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 228008] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> terminal\nN6 -> N4, N2\nN7 -> terminal\nN2 -> N0\nN9 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN1 -> N5, N2\nN4 -> N9, N1\nN8 -> N6, N3\nN3 -> N9, N7\n\nLegal moves: N6, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, the legal moves are to N6 or N3. Evaluating each:  \n- Moving to N6 leads to N4 or N2.  \n  - N4 → N9 (terminal) or N1 → N5 or N2.  \n    - N5 → terminal; N2 → N0 → terminal.  \n  - N2 → N0 → terminal.  \n  So from N6, paths eventually end; the player who moves to N6 may lose if opponent plays optimally.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to N9 (terminal) or N7 (terminal). Both are terminal. So the player who moves to N3 wins immediately, as opponent has no move.  \nThus, choosing N3 results in an immediate win. N3 is a winning move.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N8, the legal moves are to N6 or N3. Evaluating each:  \n- Moving to N6 leads to N4 or N2.  \n  - N4 → N9 (terminal) or N1 → N5 or N2.  \n    - N5 → terminal; N2 → N0 → terminal.  \n  - N2 → N0 → terminal.  \n  So from N6, paths eventually end; the player who moves to N6 may lose if opponent plays optimally.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to N9 (terminal) or N7 (terminal). Both are terminal. So the player who moves to N3 wins immediately, as opponent has no move.  \nThus, choosing N3 results in an immediate win. N3 is a winning move.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt":