swer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN8 -> N1, N2\nN4 -> N1\nN3 -> N0, N7\nN9 -> N8, N3\nN0 -> N4, N5\nN5 -> terminal\nN6 -> N8, N9\n\nLegal moves: N1, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, the player can move to N1 or N2. Both N1 and N2 lead directly to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately, forcing the opponent into no move. Thus, moving to N1 or N2 is a winning move. Since both are equally good and lead to immediate win, either is optimal. Choosing N1 is valid and safe. Therefore, the best move is to N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N8, the player can move to N1 or N2. Both N1 and N2 lead directly to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately, forcing the opponent into no move. Thus, moving to N1 or N2 is a winning move. Since both are equally good and lead to immediate win, either is optimal. Choosing N1 is valid and safe. Therefore, the best move is to N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> terminal\nN3 -> N5\nN0 -> N2, N1\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> N0, N6\nN1 -> N7, N3\nN7 -> terminal\nN9 -> N2, N8\nN5 -> terminal\nN6 -> N9, N0\n\nLegal moves: N0, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N4, the player can move to N0 or N6. We analyze each option using backward i