[2026-08-13 21:35:22] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 228008] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N5, N8, N3\nN6 -> N3, N9\nN5 -> N2\nN3 -> N4, N0\nN2 -> terminal\nN0 -> N4, N1\nN1 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> N6\n\nLegal moves: N5, N8, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the player can move to N5, N8, or N3. Evaluating each:  \n- N5 → N2 → terminal: immediate win (opponent has no move).  \n- N8 → N6 → N3 → N4 or N0 → both lead to terminal or further moves; eventually leads to opponent winning or draw.  \n- N3 → N4 or N0: N4 → terminal; N0 → N4 or N1 → both terminal. All paths eventually end.  \n\nN5 leads directly to terminal in one move, so the current player wins immediately. This is optimal. Thus, choosing N5 is best.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the player can move to N5, N8, or N3. Evaluating each:  \n- N5 → N2 → terminal: immediate win (opponent has no move).  \n- N8 → N6 → N3 → N4 or N0 → both lead to terminal or further moves; eventually leads to opponent winning or draw.  \n- N3 → N4 or N0: N4 → terminal; N0 → N4 or N1 → both terminal. All paths eventually end.  \n\nN5 leads directly to terminal in one move, so the current player wins immediately. This is optimal. Thus, choosing N5 is best.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N5, N8, N3\nN6 -> N3, N9\nN5 -> N2\nN3 -> N4, N0\nN2 -> terminal\nN0 -> N4, N1\nN1 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> N6\n\nLegal moves: N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N5, the only legal move is to N2. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N2 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N5. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the only legal move is to N2. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N2 is the only option and results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N5. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N12\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> N8, N2\nN0 -> N4, N7\nN6 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN12 -> N11, N0, N3\nN5 -> N10\nN7 -> N6, N2, N3, N4\nN13 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN10 -> terminal\nN11 -> N1\nN2 -> N9\nN8 -> N5, N13\nN9 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N11, N0, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N12, the player can move to N11, N0, or N3. N11 leads to N1, which is terminal, so the opponent has no move and wins immediately. Thus, moving to N11 results in an immediate win. Moving to N0 leads to N4 or N7; both eventually lead to terminal nodes or cycles, but N7 leads to N6 (terminal) or N2 (to N9, terminal), so the game ends. However, N11 gives the first player a winning move by forcing the opponent into a terminal node immediately. Therefore, N11 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N11</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N12, the player can move to N11, N0, or N3. N11 leads to N1, which is terminal, so the opponent has no move and wins immediately. Thus, moving to N11 results in an immediate win. Moving to N0 leads to N4 or N7; both eventually lead to terminal nodes or cycles, but N7 leads to N6 (terminal) or N2 (to N9, terminal), so the game ends. However, N11 gives the first player a winning move by forcing the opponent into a terminal node immediately. Therefore, N11 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N11</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> N8, N4\nN8 -> N6, N3\nN0 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN3 -> N4, N0\nN7 -> N5, N2\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> N9, N1\nN4 -> N0\n\nLegal moves: N5, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the player can move to N5 or N2. Evaluating each:  \n- N5 leads to N8 or N4.  \n  - N8 → N6 (terminal) or N3.  \n    - N3 → N4 or N0 (both terminal).  \n    - N4 → N0 (terminal).  \n  - N4 → N0 (terminal).  \n  Th