 to N1 ends the game and wins the game.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> N8, N4\nN8 -> N6, N3\nN0 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN3 -> N4, N0\nN7 -> N5, N2\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> N9, N1\nN4 -> N0\n\nLegal moves: N9, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N9 or N1. Both N9 and N1 lead to terminal nodes, so whichever move is made, the current player wins immediately (the opponent has no legal move). Thus, both moves result in an immediate win for the player who moves. Since both options are equivalent in outcome, either is valid. Choosing N9 is arbitrary but safe. Therefore, the optimal move is to N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N9 or N1. Both N9 and N1 lead to terminal nodes, so whichever move is made, the current player wins immediately (the opponent has no legal move). Thus, both moves result in an immediate win for the player who moves. Since both options are equivalent in outcome, either is valid. Choosing N9 is arbitrary but safe. Therefore, the optimal move is to N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reas