ses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N5, N3\nN1 -> N6, N9\nN2 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN8 -> N4\nN4 -> terminal\nN5 -> N1, N2\nN9 -> terminal\nN3 -> N5, N9\nN0 -> N8, N7\n\nLegal moves: N4assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, the only legal move is to N4, which leads to terminal. Thus, the first player (me) moves to N4 and wins immediately. No alternative move exists, so this is the only option. The outcome is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N8, the only legal move is to N4, which leads to terminal. Thus, the first player (me) moves to N4 and wins immediately. No alternative move exists, so this is the only option. The outcome is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}]
