[2026-08-13 21:37:22] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 228008] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> N6, N3\nN8 -> N9, N7, N1\nN6 -> N5, N0\nN7 -> N2\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> N1, N6\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN0 -> N4\n\nLegal moves: N9, N7, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, the player can move to N9, N7, or N1. We analyze each move for winning potential.  \n- N7 → N2 → terminal: one move, opponent loses immediately. This is a winning move.  \n- N1 → N6 or N3:  \n  - N6 → N5 → terminal or N0 → N4 → terminal: both lead to terminal, so opponent wins if they move to terminal.  \n  - N3 → terminal: immediate win for opponent. So N1 leads to opponent having a move to terminal.  \n- N9 → N1 or N6: both lead to positions where opponent can win.  \nThus, moving to N7 immediately ends the game with opponent having no move. This is optimal. Final outcome: win.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N8, the player can move to N9, N7, or N1. We analyze each move for winning potential.  \n- N7 → N2 → terminal: one move, opponent loses immediately. This is a winning move.  \n- N1 → N6 or N3:  \n  - N6 → N5 → terminal or N0 → N4 → terminal: both lead to terminal, so opponent wins if they move to terminal.  \n  - N3 → terminal: immediate win for opponent. So N1 leads to opponent having a move to terminal.  \n- N9 → N1 or N6: both lead to positions where opponent can win.  \nThus, moving to N7 immediately ends the game with opponent having no move. This is optimal. Final outcome: win.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> N6, N3\nN8 -> N9, N7, N1\nN6 -> N5, N0\nN7 -> N2\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> N1, N6\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\nN0 -> N4\n\nLegal moves: N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N2. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N2 results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N7. Therefore, N2 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N2. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N2 results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N7. Therefore, N2 is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N10\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N2, N13\nN10 -> N3, N8\nN2 -> N4, N9\nN11 -> N7, N6\nN13 -> N11, N4\nN4 -> terminal\