at maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> N3, N8\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> N0, N1\nN6 -> terminal\nN7 -> N6\nN1 -> N7, N8\nN8 -> terminal\nN4 -> N7, N9\nN2 -> terminal\nN3 -> N2, N5\n\nLegal moves: N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N6. N6 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N6 results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N7. Therefore, the optimal choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N6. N6 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N6 results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N7. Therefore, the optimal choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N0\nN4 -> N6, N1\nN2 -> N8, N3\nN7 -> terminal\nN0 -> N2, N8\nN6 -> N7\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> N5, N2\n\nLegal moves: N6, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N4, the legal moves are to N6 or N1. Evaluating each:  \n- N6 → N7 → terminal: this is a winning path (player who moves to N7 wins immediately).  \n- N1 → N5 or N2:  \n  - N5 → N9 (terminal) or N0  \n    - N9 → terminal: immediate win  \n    - N0 → N2 or N8  \n      - N2 → N8 or N3 → both lead to terminal  \n  - N2 → N8 or N3 → both terminal  \nThus, from N1, the opponent can force a win unless the path leads to a terminal. However, N6 leads directly to N7 → terminal, so the first player wins immediately. Hence, moving to N6 is optimal and ensures victory.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N4, the legal moves are to N6 or N1. Evaluating each:  \n- N6 → N7 → terminal: this is a winning path (player who moves to N7 wins immediately).  \n- N1 → N5 or N2:  \n  - N5 → N9 (terminal) or N0  \n    - N9 → terminal: immediate win  \n    - N0 → N2 or N8  \n      - N2 → N8 or N3 → both lead to terminal  \n  - N2 → N8 or N3 → both terminal  \nThus, from N1, the opponent can force a win unless the path leads to a terminal. However, N6 leads directly to N7 → terminal, so the first player wins immediately. Hence, moving to N6 is optimal and ensures victory.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N0\nN4 -> N6, N1\nN2 -> N8, N3\nN7 -> terminal\nN0 -> N2, N8\nN6 -> N7\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> N5, N2\n\nLegal moves: N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, the only legal move is to N7. N7 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N7 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N7 is the only option and results in a win. No other move is available, so this is the optimal choice.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>