ical point is that from N6, both options end in terminal immediately, so the next player has no move. Hence, moving to N6 wins immediately. Therefore, N6 is the best move.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> N6, N1\nN2 -> N12, N7\nN12 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN13 -> terminal\nN9 -> N11, N8\nN4 -> N12, N0\nN7 -> N9, N8\nN3 -> terminal\nN6 -> N13, N3\nN11 -> terminal\nN1 -> N4, N2\nN10 -> terminal\nN0 -> N10, N11\n\nLegal moves: N13, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N13 or N3. N13 and N3 are both terminal nodes. Moving to either ends the game immediately, and the player who makes the move wins (since the opponent has no move). Thus, both moves result in an immediate win for the current player. Since both options are equally optimal, either is valid. Choosing N13 is arbitrary but safe.</reason>\n<answer>N13</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N13 or N3. N13 and N3 are both terminal nodes. Moving to either ends the game immediately, and the player who makes the move wins (since the opponent has no move). Thus, both moves result in an immediate win for the current player. Since both options are equally optimal, either is valid. Choosing N13 is arbitrary but safe.</reason>\n<answer>N13</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move lo