in. It is a better choice than N0, which may require more steps and risk opponent counterplay.\n\nTherefore, the optimal move is to N11.</reason>\n<answer>N11</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the legal moves are to N0 or N11. Analyzing each:\n\n- Move to N11: leads to N6 (terminal) or N1 (terminal). Both are terminal, so the next player cannot move — current player wins. So N11 is a winning move.\n\n- Move to N0: leads to N7 or N3.\n  - N7 → N13 or N2 (both terminal) → next player loses → current player wins.\n  - N3 → N9 or N10.\n    - N9 → terminal.\n    - N10 → N9 or N4.\n      - N4 → N8 or N12 → both lead to terminal or further paths.\n      - Eventually, all paths lead to terminal states. But due to the structure, any path from N0 eventually leads to terminal nodes after a few steps, and the opponent will face no moves.\n\nHowever, both N0 and N11 eventually end in terminal states. But in N11, the immediate moves go directly to terminal nodes, so the opponent has no move — immediate win.\n\nThus, choosing N11 guarantees an immediate win. It is a better choice than N0, which may require more steps and risk opponent counterplay.\n\nTherefore, the optimal move is to N11.</reason>\n<answer>N11</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N11\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN7 -> N13, N2\nN6 -> terminal\nN10 -> N9, N4\nN11 -> N6, N1\nN13 -> terminal\nN12 -> terminal\nN8 -> N13, N12\nN1 -> terminal\nN3 -> N9, N10\nN5 -> N0, N11\nN4 -> N8, N12\nN0 -> N7, N3\n\nLegal moves: N6, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N11, the legal moves are to N6 or N1. N6 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately. N1 also leads to terminal, so moving to N1 also wins immediately. Both moves end the game immediately, so either is a winning move. Since both result in an immediate win, either is optimal. Choosing N6 is valid and terminal. Thus, the best choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N11, the legal moves are to N6 or N1. N6 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately. N1 also leads to terminal, so moving to N1 also wins immediately. Both moves end the game immediately, so either is a winning move. Since both result in an immediate win, either is optimal. Choosing N6 is valid and terminal. Thus, the best choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}]
