e optimal move is N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN10 -> N9, N0\nN6 -> N11, N13\nN12 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> N10, N2\nN0 -> N6, N7\nN13 -> N1, N12\nN11 -> N1, N3\nN3 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> N6, N5\nN1 -> terminal\nN7 -> N3, N8\n\nLegal moves: N10, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N5, the legal moves are to N10 or N2. N2 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N2 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the legal moves are to N10 or N2. N2 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N2 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> N10, N13\nN8 -> N11, N0\nN3 -> N11, N8\nN2 -> N5, N3\nN13 -> N7, N6\nN1 -> N9, N2\nN0 -> N4, N7\nN6 -> terminal\nN9 -> N12, N10\nN4 -> terminal\nN12 -> terminal\nN11 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN10 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N12, N10assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N12 or N10. Both N12 and N10 lead to terminal nodes, meaning the player who moves to either wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, either move ends the game on the next turn, and the current player wins. Since both options result in an immediate win, either is optimal. Choosing N10 is valid and sufficient.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N12 or N10. Both N12 and N10 lead to terminal nodes, meaning the player who moves to either wins immediately (the opponent has no move). Thus, either move ends the game on the next turn, and the current player wins. Since both options result in an immediate win, either is optimal. Choosing N10 is valid and sufficient.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N9\nN6 -> N4, N0\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> N2, N7\nN4 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> N3, N1\nN3 -> N4, N1\nN1 -> N6, N8\n\nLegal moves: N2, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N5, the player can move to N2 or N7. N7 leads to N9, which leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N7 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N7 ends the game in one step, and the opponent has no move. Moving to N2 leads to a subtree with branching options, which may allow the opponent to respond. Since N7 results in an immediate win (opponent cannot move), choosing N7 is optimal. Therefore, the best move is to N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the player can move to N2 or N7. N7 leads to N9, which leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N7 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N7 ends the game in one step, and the opponent has no move. Moving to N2 leads to a subtree with branching options, which may allow the opponent to respond. Since N7 results in an immediate win (opponent cannot move), choosing N7 is optimal. Therefore, the best move is to N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N9\nN6 -> N4, N0\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> N2, N7\nN4 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> N3, N1\nN3 -> N4, N1\nN1 -> N6, N8\n\nLegal moves: N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N9. N9 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N9 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N9 is the only legal and optimal move. No further moves are available after that, so the current player wins.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N9. N9 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N9 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N9 is the only legal and optimal move. No further moves are available after that, so the current player wins.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geo