oves to N6 (terminal), N7 (terminal), N1. N1 leads to N8 (terminal), so all paths eventually end in terminal nodes. This results in a chain that eventually ends with a losing position for the opponent. \n- Move to N5: N5 → N9 → (as above), which again leads into a long chain. \n- Move to N0: N0 → N2 (terminal), so opponent loses immediately. This is a direct win.\n\nThus, moving to N0 immediately ends the game with the opponent having no legal move. This is optimal. The best move is to N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> N6, N7, N1\nN4 -> N9, N5, N0\nN9 -> N3, N8\nN2 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9\nN8 -> terminal\nN0 -> N2\nN6 -> terminal\nN1 -> N8\n\nLegal moves: N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N2 or N4 (since N0 -> N2 and N0 has no other outgoing edges listed). N2 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N2 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N2 or N4 (since N0 -> N2 and N0 has no other outgoing edges listed). N2 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N2 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed 