[2026-08-13 22:58:13] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 228008] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN12 -> N1, N11\nN1 -> N8, N9\nN8 -> N4, N2\nN9 -> N5, N13\nN4 -> N3, N5\nN10 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN6 -> N12, N10\nN3 -> terminal\nN13 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN11 -> N2, N7\nN0 -> N1, N6\nN5 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N1, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the player can move to N1 or N6. N1 leads to N8 or N9, both of which eventually lead to terminals or to N5, N13, etc., with paths that do not offer strong control. N6 leads to N12 or N10. N10 leads to terminal immediately. N12 leads to N1 or N11. N11 leads to N2 or N7, both terminals. So, from N0 moving to N6 offers a direct path to terminal via N10, and even if it goes to N12, it branches into dead ends. Thus, moving to N6 gives immediate control and limits opponent's options. Hence, choosing N6 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the player can move to N1 or N6. N1 leads to N8 or N9, both of which eventually lead to terminals or to N5, N13, etc., with paths that do not offer strong control. N6 leads to N12 or N10. N10 leads to terminal immediately. N12 leads to N1 or N11. N11 leads to N2 or N7, both terminals. So, from N0 moving to N6 offers a direct path to terminal via N10, and even if it goes to N12, it branches into dead ends. Thus, moving to N6 gives immediate control and limits opponent's options. Hence, choosing N6 maximizes the outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN12 -> N1, N11\nN1 -> N8, N9\nN8 -> N4, N2\nN9 -> N5, N13\nN4 -> N3, N5\nN10 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN6 -> N12, N10\nN3 -> terminal\nN13 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN11 -> N2, N7\nN0 -> N1, N6\nN5 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N12, N10assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N12 or N10. N10 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N10 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N10 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N10.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N12 or N10. N10 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N10 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N10 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N10.</reason>\n<answer>N10</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N8, N3\nN3 -> N9, N6\nN7 -> N2, N0\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> N5, N8\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN8 -> N7\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> N4, N5\n\nLegal moves: N8, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, player can move to N8 or N3. N3 leads to N9 or N6; N6 and N9 eventually lead to terminal or cycles. N8 leads to N7, which leads to N2 or N0, both terminal. Thus, from N1, moving to N3 gives immediate access to terminal (via N6 or N9→N5), which ends the game immediately. From N1→N8→N7→N2 or N0, the game continues, giving opponent chance to move. N1→N3 gives a path where either N3→N6 or N3→N9→N5 leads to terminal, so the first player can force a win. The move to N3 maximizes immediate outcome. Thus, optimal choice is N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, player can move to N8 or N3. N3 leads to N9 or N6; N6 and N9 eventually lead to terminal or cycles. N8 leads to N7, which leads to N2 or N0, both terminal. Thus, from N1, moving to N3 gives immediate access to terminal (via N6 or N9→N5), which ends the game immediately. From N1→N8→N7→N2 or N0, the game continues, giving opponent chance to move. N1→N3 gives a path where either N3→N6 or N3→N9→N5 leads to terminal, so the first player can force a win. The move to N3 maximizes immediate outcome. Thus, optimal choice is N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N8, N3\nN3 -> N9, N6\nN7 -> N2, N0\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> N5, N8\nN6 -> terminal\nN0 -> terminal\nN8 -> N7\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> N4, N5\n\nLegal moves: N9, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N9 or N6. N6 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N6 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N9 or N6. N6 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N6 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N6 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN3 -> N5\nN2 -> N3, N7\nN8 -> N4, N1\nN7 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> N9, N2\nN4 -> N6\nN5 -> terminal\nN0 -> N1, N4, N8\n\nLegal moves: N1, N4, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the player can move to N1, N4, or N8. We analyze each move to determine the outcome. \n\n- Move to N1: leads to N9 (terminal) or N2. From N2, can go to N3 or N7. Both N3→N5 (terminal) and N7→terminal end the game. This chain leads to terminal outcomes; thus, the player who moves to N1 risks being in a losing position if the opponent plays optimally.\n- Move to N4: leads to N6 → terminal. This is a direct end, so the opponent cannot move. This is a winning move: the first player ends the game immediately.\n- Move to N8: leads to N4 or N1. Both paths eventually lead to terminal or branching, but since N4 leads to terminal, and N1 branches, this gives opponent more flexibility, making it suboptimal.\n\nThe move to N4 leads to immediate terminal win. Therefore, choosing N4 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the player can move to N1, N4, or N8. We analyze each move to determine the outcome. \n\n- Move to N1: leads to N9 (terminal) or N2. From N2, can go to N3 or N7. Both N3→N5 (terminal) and N7→terminal end the game. This chain leads to terminal outcomes; thus, the player who moves to N1 risks being in a losing position if the opponent plays optimally.\n- Move to N4: leads to N6 → terminal. This is a direct end, so the opponent cannot move. This is a winning move: the first player ends the game immediately.\n- Move to N8: leads to N4 or N1. Both paths eventually lead to terminal or branching, but since N4 leads to terminal, and N1 branches, this gives opponent more flexibility, making it suboptimal.\n\nThe move to N4 leads to immediate terminal win. Therefore, choosing N4 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN6 -> terminal\nN3 -> N5\nN2 -> N3, N7\nN8 -> N4, N1\nN7 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN1 -> N9, N2\nN4 -> N6\nN5 -> terminal\nN0 -> N1, N4, N8\n\nLegal moves: N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N4, the only legal move is to N6, which leads to terminal. Thus, the current player wins immediately. No further moves are needed. The optimal choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N4, the only legal move is to N6, which leads to terminal. Thus, the current player wins immediately. No further moves are needed. The optimal choice is N6.</reason>\n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N1, N5\nN11 -> terminal\nN10 -> terminal\nN4 -> N12, N1\nN1 -> terminal\nN13 -> N2, N8\nN0 -> N13, N7\nN9 -> N3, N11\nN2 -> terminal\nN7 -> N11, N10\nN6 -> N0, N9\nN5 -> N10, N4\nN12 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N0, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N0 or N9.  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N13, which branches to N2 (terminal) or N8. From N8, moves to N1 (terminal) or N5. N5 leads to N10 (terminal) or N4; N4 leads to N12 (terminal) or N1 (terminal). All branches eventually end.  \n- Moving to N9 leads to N3 (terminal) or N11 (terminal). Both are terminal.  \nFrom N6 → N9, immediate terminal win (next player loses).  \nFrom N6 → N0, the game continues, but due to branching and no immediate loss, N9 is a better move since it ends immediately.  \nThus, choosing N9 results in immediate win (next player loses). So optimal choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N0 or N9.  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N13, which branches to N2 (terminal) or N8. From N8, moves to N1 (terminal) or N5. N5 leads to N10 (terminal) or N4; N4 leads to N12 (terminal) or N1 (terminal). All branches eventually end.  \n- Moving to N9 leads to N3 (terminal) or N11 (terminal). Both are terminal.  \nFrom N6 → N9, immediate terminal win (next player loses).  \nFrom N6 → N0, the game continues, but due to branching and no immediate loss, N9 is a better move since it ends immediately.  \nThus, choosing N9 results in immediate win (next player loses). So optimal choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N1, N5\nN11 -> terminal\nN10 -> terminal\nN4 -> N12, N1\nN1 -> terminal\nN13 -> N2, N8\nN0 -> N13, N7\nN9 -> N3, N11\nN2 -> terminal\nN7 -> N11, N10\nN6 -> N0, N9\nN5 -> N10, N4\nN12 -> terminal\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N3, N11assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, the player can move to N3 or N11. N3 leads directly to terminal, so the current player wins immediately. N11 also leads to terminal, so moving to N11 also wins immediately. Both moves result in an immediate win. Thus, either is optimal. Choosing N3 is sufficient and direct.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N9, the player can move to N3 or N11. N3 leads directly to terminal, so the current player wins immediately. N11 also leads to terminal, so moving to N11 also wins immediately. Both moves result in an immediate win. Thus, either is optimal. Choosing N3 is sufficient and direct.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N5\nN9 -> N2, N7\nN0 -> terminal\nN6 -> N7, N2, N9\nN2 -> N1, N4\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N0, N3\nN1 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN3 -> N8\n\nLegal moves: N7, N2, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N7, N2, or N9. We analyze each:  \n- N7 → N5 → terminal: First player wins immediately (opponent loses).  \n- N2 → N1 or N4: N1 → terminal, N4 → N0 or N3. N0 or N3 leads to N8 (terminal), so chain ends. If player reaches N4, opponent can go to terminal. But if player moves to N4, opponent can go to N3 → N8 → terminal, so opponent wins. So from N2, game ends in 1–2 steps.  \n- N9 → N2 or N7. From N2 or N7, game continues, but both eventually lead to terminal.  \n\nThe move to N7 (to N5) ends immediately with opponent having no move. That's a win. So choosing N7 maximizes outcome. Thus, best choice is N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N7, N2, or N9. We analyze each:  \n- N7 → N5 → terminal: First player wins immediately (opponent loses).  \n- N2 → N1 or N4: N1 → terminal, N4 → N0 or N3. N0 or N3 leads to N8 (terminal), so chain ends. If player reaches N4, opponent can go to terminal. But if player moves to N4, opponent can go to N3 → N8 → terminal, so opponent wins. So from N2, game ends in 1–2 steps.  \n- N9 → N2 or N7. From N2 or N7, game continues, but both eventually lead to terminal.  \n\nThe move to N7 (to N5) ends immediately with opponent having no move. That's a win. So choosing N7 maximizes outcome. Thus, best choice is N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N5\nN9 -> N2, N7\nN0 -> terminal\nN6 -> N7, N2, N9\nN2 -> N1, N4\nN5 -> terminal\nN4 -> N0, N3\nN1 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN3 -> N8\n\nLegal moves: N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N5. N5 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N5 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N5 ends the game on the next player's turn, and the current player wins. No other move from N7 is available. Therefore, the optimal choice is N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N5. N5 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N5 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N5 ends the game on the next player's turn, and the current player wins. No other move from N7 is available. Therefore, the optimal choice is N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}]
