rminal in one move, it ends the game immediately. The game is won by the player who forces opponent to move to terminal.  \nTherefore, from N4, choosing N1 gives immediate end of game (opponent has no move), so it is optimal. Hence, best move is N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN0 -> terminal\nN7 -> N8, N6\nN2 -> N9, N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN1 -> N0, N3\nN4 -> N2, N1\nN5 -> terminal\nN6 -> N0\nN9 -> N5, N7\n\nLegal moves: N0, N3assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal moves are to N0 or N3. N3 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N3 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N3 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal moves are to N0 or N3. N3 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N3 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N3 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N3.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected grap