e legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN11 -> N9, N12\nN10 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> N4\nN7 -> N12\nN13 -> N2, N8, N0\nN1 -> N7, N10\nN4 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN3 -> N0, N13, N7\nN2 -> terminal\nN8 -> N6, N1\nN0 -> N5, N11\nN12 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N0, N13, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N0, N13, or N7. We evaluate each:\n\n- Move to N7: leads to N12 (terminal), so the opponent has no move → immediate win.\n- Move to N13: leads to choices (N2, N8, N0). N2 and N0 lead to terminal or further paths. N8 leads to N6 (terminal) or N1. N1 leads to N7 or N10 (both eventually lead to terminal or back to branches). But from N13, opponent can play into branching paths, potentially creating long chains. However, the key is: if we go to N7, it's terminal. But N7 → N12 (terminal), so player after us loses immediately.\n\nIf we go to N7 → game ends after our move → opponent loses immediately → this is a win.\n\nThus, playing to N7 is a direct win. No need to explore further.\n\nTherefore, best move is to N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the legal moves are to N0, N13, or N7. We evaluate each:\n\n- Move to N7: leads to N12 (terminal), so the opponent has no move → immediate win.\n- Move to N13: leads to choices (N2, N8, N0). N2 and N0 lead to terminal or further paths. N8 leads to N6 (terminal) or N1. N1 leads to N7 or N10 (both eventually lead to terminal or back to branches). But from N13, opponent can play into branching paths, potentially creating long chains. However, the key is: if we go to N7, it's terminal. But N7 → N12 (terminal), so player after us loses im