nal state in one move — meaning the current player wins immediately. Thus, choosing N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> N6, N0\nN9 -> N8\nN6 -> terminal\nN3 -> N9, N5\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN8 -> N1, N7\nN7 -> N4, N2\nN4 -> N1, N0\n\nLegal moves: N6, N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N5, the legal moves are to N6 or N0. N0 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N0 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the legal moves are to N6 or N0. N0 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N0 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> terminal\nN9 -> N1, N3\nN13 -> terminal\nN4 -> N6, N12\nN2 -> N4, N5\nN10 -> N11, N0\nN1 -> N8, N11\nN5 -> N10, N13\nN11 -> terminal\nN8 -> terminal\nN6 -> N9, N8\nN0 -> terminal\nN12 -> N7, N0\nN3 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N4, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N4 or N5. Evaluating both:\n\n- Move to N4: leads to N6 or N12. \n  - N6 → N9 or N8 (N8 is terminal; N9 → N1 or N3, both eventually lead to terminals or cycles with terminal outcomes).\n  - N12 → N7 or N0 (both lead to terminal states). These chains are mostly losing.\n- Move to N5: leads to N10 or N13.\n  - N13 → terminal (winning end).\n  - N10 → N11 or N0 (N11 → terminal, so both end in terminal).\n  - Thus, N5 branch offers terminal win path via N13.\n\nThus, choosing N5 ensures a path to terminal with no immediate risk. N5 leads to a winning outcome via N13. So optimal move is N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the legal moves are to N4 or N5. Evaluating both:\n\n- Move to N4: leads to N6 or N12. \n  - N6 → N9 or N8 (N8 is terminal; N9 → N1 or N3, both eventually lead to terminals or cycles with terminal outcomes).\n  - N12 → N7 or N0 (both lead to terminal states). These chains are mostly losing.\n- Move to N5: leads to N10 or N13.\n  - N13 → terminal (winning end).\n  - N10 → N11 or N0 (N11 → terminal, so both end in terminal).\n  - Thus, N5 branch offers terminal win path via N13.\n\nThus, choosing N5 ensures a path to terminal with no immediate risk. N5 leads to a winning outcome via N13. So optimal move is N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected gra