e, the optimal choice is N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> terminal\nN3 -> N6, N1, N2\nN6 -> N5, N0\nN4 -> N8\nN0 -> N9, N4\nN9 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN1 -> N7\nN2 -> N1, N6\n\nLegal moves: N6, N1, N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the player can move to N6, N1, or N2. We evaluate each move:  \n- N6 leads to N5 or N0: N5 ends the game immediately (win for next player), N0 leads to N9 or N4 (both eventually loop or end).  \n- N1 leads to N7 (terminal, immediate loss for next player).  \n- N2 leads to N1 or N6 (N1 leads to terminal, N6 continues).  \n\nAnalyzing outcomes:  \n- Move to N1: next player moves to N7 (terminal), so current player wins.  \n- Move to N2: next player can go to N1 (win) or N6 (continue).  \n- Move to N6: next player can go to N5 (win) or N0 (loop).  \n\nBest choice: Move to N1, forcing opponent into terminal move (loss). This maximizes immediate outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the player can move to N6, N1, or N2. We evaluate each move:  \n- N6 leads to N5 or N0: N5 ends the game immediately (win for next player), N0 leads to N9 or N4 (both eventually loop or end).  \n- N1 leads to N7 (terminal, immediate loss for next player).  \n- N2 leads to N1 or N6 (N1 leads to terminal, N6 continues).  \n\nAnalyzing outcomes:  \n- Move to N1: next player moves to N7 (terminal), so current player wins.  \n- Move to N2: next player can go to N1 (win) or N6 (continue).  \n- Move to N6: next player can go to N5 (win) or N0 (loop).  \n\nBest choice: Move to N1, forcing opponent into terminal move (loss). This maximizes immediate outcome.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN9 -> terminal\nN7 -> N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN3 -> N8, N9\nN2 -> terminal\nN6 -> N0, N5\nN8 -> terminal\nN1 -> N6, N7, N4\nN4 -> N6\nN5 -> N3, N0\n\nLegal moves: N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N2. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N2 results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N7. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the only legal move is to N2. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N2 results in an immediate win. No other move is available from N7. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent n