iate win.  \n\nThus, choosing N7 gives a direct terminal win. No need to explore further due to immediate terminal moves. The best move is to N7.</reason>  \n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal moves are to N13 or N7. Evaluating outcomes:  \n- Move to N13: leads to N8 or N9.  \n  - N8 → N5 (to terminal) or N11 (terminal) → safe win.  \n  - N9 → N10 (terminal) or N4.  \n    - N4 → N12 (terminal) or N3 → N2 or N12 → eventually loops back or ends.  \n    - Risk of entering cycles or long paths.  \n- Move to N7: leads to N0 (terminal) or N6 (terminal) → immediate win.  \n\nThus, choosing N7 gives a direct terminal win. No need to explore further due to immediate terminal moves. The best move is to N7.</reason>  \n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> N10, N4\nN10 -> terminal\nN4 -> N12, N3\nN1 -> N13, N7\nN7 -> N0, N6\nN6 -> terminal\nN2 -> N6, N11\nN13 -> N8, N9\nN8 -> N5, N11\nN11 -> terminal\nN12 -> terminal\nN3 -> N2, N12\nN0 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N0, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N0 or N6. Both N0 and N6 lead to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately. Thus, any move from N7 ends the game on the next turn. Therefore, the optimal choice is either N0 or N6. Since both are terminal winning moves, either is valid. We select N0 as it appears first in the list.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N0 or N6. Both N0 and N6 lead to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately. Thus, any move from N7 ends the game on the next turn. Therefore, the optimal choice is either N0 or N6. Since both are terminal winning moves, either is valid. We select N0 as it appears first in the list.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}]
