[2026-08-13 23:31:01] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 228008] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> N6\nN7 -> N5, N4, N8\nN8 -> N9\nN1 -> terminal\nN0 -> N8, N3, N1\nN3 -> terminal\nN5 -> N0\nN4 -> N2, N5\nN6 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N5, N4, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N5, N4, or N8. Analyze each:\n\n- N5 leads to N0, then from N0 to N8, N3, or N1. N3 and N1 are terminal, so the game continues to N8 → N9 (terminal). This path leads to opponent's turn eventually, and due to dependency chains, N5 path is long and can be drawn out but ends with a win condition depending on parity.\n- N4 leads to N2 or N5. N2 → N6 (terminal), N5 → N0 → loop or end. Path is volatile but eventually leads to terminal.\n- N8 → N9 (terminal), so immediate end, and the player who moves to N8 causes the opponent to face the end.\n\nThus, moving to N8 ends the game immediately (next player loses). This is a forced win.\n\nTherefore, choosing N8 is optimal because it results in the opponent having no move, winning immediately.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N5, N4, or N8. Analyze each:\n\n- N5 leads to N0, then from N0 to N8, N3, or N1. N3 and N1 are terminal, so the game continues to N8 → N9 (terminal). This path leads to opponent's turn eventually, and due to dependency chains, N5 path is long and can be drawn out but ends with a win condition depending on parity.\n- N4 leads to N2 or N5. N2 → N6 (terminal), N5 → N0 → loop or end. Path is volatile but eventually leads to terminal.\n- N8 → N9 (terminal), so immediate end, and the player who moves to N8 causes the opponent to face the end.\n\nThus, moving to N8 ends the game immediately (next player loses). This is a forced win.\n\nTherefore, choosing N8 is optimal because it results in the opponent having no move, winning immediately.</reason>\n<answer>N8</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN2 -> N6\nN7 -> N5, N4, N8\nN8 -> N9\nN1 -> terminal\nN0 -> N8, N3, N1\nN3 -> terminal\nN5 -> N0\nN4 -> N2, N5\nN6 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>The current node is N8. From N8, the only legal move is to N9. N9 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N9 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N9 is the only legal and optimal move. Therefore, the best choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>The current node is N8. From N8, the only legal move is to N9. N9 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N9 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N9 is the only legal and optimal move. Therefore, the best choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N4\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> terminal\nN0 -> N9, N6\nN1 -> terminal\nN9 -> N7, N2\nN3 -> N8, N1\nN6 -> terminal\nN5 -> N0, N3\nN7 -> N8\nN4 -> N7, N5\nN2 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N7, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N4, the legal moves are to N7 or N5. N7 leads to N8, which is terminal, so the player who moves to N7 wins immediately. N5 leads to N0 or N3. N0 branches to N9 or N6; N6 leads to terminal, so that is a losing move if the opponent can force a win. From N3, one can reach N8 or N1, both leading to terminal or winning positions. Thus, moving to N7 ensures immediate win. Therefore, optimal move is to N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N4, the legal moves are to N7 or N5. N7 leads to N8, which is terminal, so the player who moves to N7 wins immediately. N5 leads to N0 or N3. N0 branches to N9 or N6; N6 leads to terminal, so that is a losing move if the opponent can force a win. From N3, one can reach N8 or N1, both leading to terminal or winning positions. Thus, moving to N7 ensures immediate win. Therefore, optimal move is to N7.</reason>\n<answer>N7</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> terminal\nN5 -> N9, N2\nN2 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN6 -> N1, N3\nN3 -> N7\nN4 -> terminal\nN9 -> N4, N2\nN0 -> N6, N5\nN8 -> N0, N9\n\nLegal moves: N0, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, the legal moves are to N0 or N9. Evaluating each path:  \n- Move to N0: N0 → N6 or N5.  \n   - N6 → N1 or N3; both lead to terminal or N3 → N7 → terminal.  \n   - N5 → N9 or N2; N2 → terminal, N9 → N4 or N2 (both terminal). All branches end.  \n   This branch has limited depth and no cycles, leading to eventual loss if opponent plays well.  \n- Move to N9: N9 → N4 or N2 (both terminal). Direct end.  \n\nHowever, from N8 → N9, the next player is at N4 or N2, both terminal — thus the player who moves to N9 wins immediately. But actually, once a player moves into a terminal node, the next player loses. So N9 leads to immediate end of turn, and opponent loses. So, move to N9 gives the current player a winning move. Thus, optimal move is N9. Therefore, the choice that maximizes outcome is N9.</reason>  \n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N8, the legal moves are to N0 or N9. Evaluating each path:  \n- Move to N0: N0 → N6 or N5.  \n   - N6 → N1 or N3; both lead to terminal or N3 → N7 → terminal.  \n   - N5 → N9 or N2; N2 → terminal, N9 → N4 or N2 (both terminal). All branches end.  \n   This branch has limited depth and no cycles, leading to eventual loss if opponent plays well.  \n- Move to N9: N9 → N4 or N2 (both terminal). Direct end.  \n\nHowever, from N8 → N9, the next player is at N4 or N2, both terminal — thus the player who moves to N9 wins immediately. But actually, once a player moves into a terminal node, the next player loses. So N9 leads to immediate end of turn, and opponent loses. So, move to N9 gives the current player a winning move. Thus, optimal move is N9. Therefore, the choice that maximizes outcome is N9.</reason>  \n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N9\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> N1, N6\nN5 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN8 -> N5\nN6 -> N0, N2\nN9 -> N3, N1\nN1 -> N5, N7\nN0 -> N4, N8\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N3, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N9, the player can move to N3 or N1.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to N1 or N6.  \n  - N1 leads to N5 (terminal) or N7 (terminal) → opponent wins.  \n  - N6 leads to N0 or N2.  \n    - N0 → N4 or N8 → N8 → N5 (terminal).  \n    - N2 → terminal.  \n    So paths from N6 eventually lead to terminal or short cycles, but ultimately opponent wins due to no back options.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N5 or N7 (both terminal), so immediate loss for opponent → current player wins.  \nThus, choosing N1 leads to immediate terminal paths for opponent.  \nTherefore, best move is N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N9, the player can move to N3 or N1.  \n- Moving to N3 leads to N1 or N6.  \n  - N1 leads to N5 (terminal) or N7 (terminal) → opponent wins.  \n  - N6 leads to N0 or N2.  \n    - N0 → N4 or N8 → N8 → N5 (terminal).  \n    - N2 → terminal.  \n    So paths from N6 eventually lead to terminal or short cycles, but ultimately opponent wins due to no back options.  \n- Moving to N1 leads to N5 or N7 (both terminal), so immediate loss for opponent → current player wins.  \nThus, choosing N1 leads to immediate terminal paths for opponent.  \nTherefore, best move is N1.</reason>\n<answer>N1</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal