oice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N9, the legal moves are to N4 or N2. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N2 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> N1, N6\nN5 -> terminal\nN7 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN8 -> N5\nN6 -> N0, N2\nN9 -> N3, N1\nN1 -> N5, N7\nN0 -> N4, N8\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N5, N7assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal moves are to N5 or N7. Both N5 and N7 lead directly to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately. Thus, any move from N1 ends the game on the next player's turn, and the current player wins. Therefore, both moves are winning. Since the goal is to maximize outcome and both result in an immediate win, either is optimal. Choosing N5 is valid and terminal. However, due to symmetry and equal outcome, either choice is fine. We select N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N1, the legal moves are to N5 or N7. Both N5 and N7 lead directly to terminal nodes, so the player who moves to either wins immediately. Thus, any move from N1 ends the game on the next player's turn, and the current player wins. Therefore, both moves are winning. Since the goal is to maximize outcome and both result in an immediate win, either is optimal. Choosing N5 is valid and terminal. However, due to symmetry and equal outcome, either choice is fine. We select N5.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N9, N1\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> N5, N3\nN6 -> N8, N4\nN9 -> N0, N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> N2\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN7 -> N6, N5\n\nLegal moves: N6, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the player can move to either N6 or N5. N5 leads to N2, which leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N5 wins immediately. Moving to N6 leads to N8 or N4. N8 leads to N9 or N1; N9 leads to N0 or N2 (N0 and N2 are terminal), and N1 is terminal. N4 leads to N5 or N3 (both eventually terminal). All paths from N6 eventually reach terminal nodes, and the second player can force a win from any branching path unless the first player can end the game immediately. Since N5 leads directly to a terminal state (via N2), the first player can choose N5 and end the game immediately, winning. Thus, choosing N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the player can move to either N6 or N5. N5 leads to N2, which leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N5 wins immediately. Moving to N6 leads to N8 or N4. N8 leads to N9 or N1; N9 leads to N0 or N2 (N0 and N2 are terminal), and N1 is terminal. N4 leads to N5 or N3 (both eventually terminal). All paths from N6 eventually reach terminal nodes, and the second player can force a win from any branching path unless the first player can end the game immediately. Since N5 leads directly to a terminal state (via N2), the first player can choose N5 and end the game immediately, winning. Thus, choosing N5 is optimal.</reason>\n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N9, N1\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> N5, N3\nN6 -> N8, N4\nN9 -> N0, N2\nN0 -> terminal\nN5 -> N2\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> terminal\nN7 -> N6, N5\n\nLegal moves: N2assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N5, the only legal move is to N2. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N2 ends the game on the next player's turn, making the current player win. No other move is available from N5. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the only legal move is to N2. N2 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N2 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N2 ends the game on the next player's turn, making the current player win. No other move is available from N5. Therefore, the optimal choice is N2.</reason>\n<answer>N2</answer>"}]
