[2026-08-13 23:45:32] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 228008] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N1\nN9 -> terminal\nN3 -> N9, N7\nN1 -> terminal\nN6 -> N0, N5\nN7 -> N2, N4\nN0 -> N7, N3\nN5 -> N9, N8\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N0, N5assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N0 or N5. Analyzing the outcomes:  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N7 or N3.  \n  - From N7: moves to N2 (terminal, loss) or N4 (terminal, loss) — opponent wins.  \n  - From N3: leads to N9 (win) or N7 (leads to loss). N9 is terminal; N7 leads to opponent's advantage. So, branching leads to a losing position.  \n  - So, N0 is risky; the game often leads to opponent control.  \n- Moving to N5 leads to N9 (terminal) or N8 → N1 → terminal. Both are terminal, so the player to move after N5 has no valid move — thus, the next player loses. So, N5 leads to immediate win (current player wins).  \nThus, choosing N5 ensures immediate end of game with no legal move for opponent. Hence, N5 is optimal.</reason>  \n<answer>N5</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N0 or N5. Analyzing the outcomes:  \n- Moving to N0 leads to N7 or N3.  \n  - From N7: moves to N2 (terminal, loss) or N4 (terminal, loss) — opponent wins.  \n  - From N3: leads to N9 (win) or N7 (leads to loss). N9 is terminal; N7 leads to opponent's advantage. So, branching leads to a losing position.  \n  - So, N0 is risky; the game often leads to opponent control.  \n- Moving to N5 leads to N9 (terminal) or N8 → N1 → terminal. Both are terminal, so the player to move after N5 has no valid move — thus, the next player loses. So, N5 leads to immediate win (current player wins).  \nThus, choosing N5 ensures immediate end of game with no legal move for opponent. Hence, N5 is optimal.</reason>  \n<answer>N5</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N5\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N1\nN9 -> terminal\nN3 -> N9, N7\nN1 -> terminal\nN6 -> N0, N5\nN7 -> N2, N4\nN0 -> N7, N3\nN5 -> N9, N8\nN2 -> terminal\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N9, N8assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N5, the legal moves are to N9 or N8. N9 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N9 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N9 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 1.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N5, the legal moves are to N9 or N8. N9 leads directly to terminal, so the player who moves to N9 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N9 is a winning move. Therefore, the optimal choice is N9.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N7\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N3\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN7 -> N4, N3, N1\nN6 -> N9\nN4 -> N2, N8, N5\nN3 -> N0\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> N6, N9\n\nLegal moves: N4, N3, N1assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N4, N3, or N1. Analyze terminal outcomes from each move:  \n- N7 → N3: leads to N0 (terminal) → next player loses → current player wins.  \n- N7 → N1: leads to N3 → N0 → opponent wins → current player loses.  \n- N7 → N4: leads to N2 (terminal), N8, or N5.  \n   - N4 → N2: terminal → opponent wins.  \n   - N4 → N5: terminal → opponent wins.  \n   - N4 → N8 → N6 → N9 (terminal) or N8 → N9 (terminal): all lead to opponent winning eventually.  \nOnly move to N3 is a winning move directly to terminal. Thus, choosing N3 wins immediately.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N7, the legal moves are to N4, N3, or N1. Analyze terminal outcomes from each move:  \n- N7 → N3: leads to N0 (terminal) → next player loses → current player wins.  \n- N7 → N1: leads to N3 → N0 → opponent wins → current player loses.  \n- N7 → N4: leads to N2 (terminal), N8, or N5.  \n   - N4 → N2: terminal → opponent wins.  \n   - N4 → N5: terminal → opponent wins.  \n   - N4 → N8 → N6 → N9 (terminal) or N8 → N9 (terminal): all lead to opponent winning eventually.  \nOnly move to N3 is a winning move directly to terminal. Thus, choosing N3 wins immediately.</reason>\n<answer>N3</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N3\n\nDirected graph:\nN1 -> N3\nN0 -> terminal\nN2 -> terminal\nN7 -> N4, N3, N1\nN6 -> N9\nN4 -> N2, N8, N5\nN3 -> N0\nN5 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN8 -> N6, N9\n\nLegal moves: N0assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N3, the only legal move is to N0. N0 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N0 ends the game on the next player's turn, making the current player win. Therefore, the optimal move is to N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N3, the only legal move is to N0. N0 leads to terminal, so the player who moves to N0 wins immediately. Thus, moving to N0 ends the game on the next player's turn, making the current player win. Therefore, the optimal move is to N0.</reason>\n<answer>N0</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N8\n\nDirected graph:\nN4 -> terminal\nN0 -> N7, N11\nN5 -> terminal\nN11 -> terminal\nN1 -> N10, N2\nN13 -> N4, N0\nN3 -> terminal\nN6 -> terminal\nN9 -> terminal\nN2 -> N6, N13\nN8 -> N1, N12\nN10 -> N6, N4\nN7 -> N3, N11\nN12 -> N5, N9\n\nLegal moves: N1, N12assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N8, the player can move to N1 or N12. Evaluating outcomes:  \n- Move to N1: leads to N10 or N2.  \n  - N10 → N6 or N4 (both terminal or win via path to terminal).  \n  - N2 → N6 or N13; N13 → N4 or N0. N0 leads to N7 or N11, which both lead to terminal paths. Eventually, all paths feed into terminal nodes. This is a losing path due to