[2026-08-13 23:57:20] [agentic_pipeline.py (516)] [INFO] [DRIVER 0 / 1][PID 228008] [{"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N0\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N7\nN5 -> N3, N1\nN9 -> terminal\nN0 -> N2, N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN2 -> N5, N1\nN6 -> N4, N9\nN7 -> terminal\nN1 -> N8, N7\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N2, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N2 or N6. Evaluating outcomes:  \n- Move to N2: Path branches to N5 or N1.  \n   - N5 leads to N3 (terminal) or N1 (looping).  \n   - N1 leads to N8 → N7 (terminal) or N7 (terminal), looping back to N8 or N7. This creates a cycle involving N8, N7, and N1, which can be exploited by the opponent.  \n   - Eventually, if looped, the second player can force a win due to parity.  \n- Move to N6: Leads to N4 (terminal) or N9 (terminal). Both end immediately, giving immediate win for the player making the move. This is a safe, terminal path.  \n\nThus, choosing N6 leads to immediate end of game and victory. N6 is optimal.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>", "episode_score": -0.95, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N0, the legal moves are to N2 or N6. Evaluating outcomes:  \n- Move to N2: Path branches to N5 or N1.  \n   - N5 leads to N3 (terminal) or N1 (looping).  \n   - N1 leads to N8 → N7 (terminal) or N7 (terminal), looping back to N8 or N7. This creates a cycle involving N8, N7, and N1, which can be exploited by the opponent.  \n   - Eventually, if looped, the second player can force a win due to parity.  \n- Move to N6: Leads to N4 (terminal) or N9 (terminal). Both end immediately, giving immediate win for the player making the move. This is a safe, terminal path.  \n\nThus, choosing N6 leads to immediate end of game and victory. N6 is optimal.</reason>  \n<answer>N6</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N6\n\nDirected graph:\nN8 -> N7\nN5 -> N3, N1\nN9 -> terminal\nN0 -> N2, N6\nN3 -> terminal\nN2 -> N5, N1\nN6 -> N4, N9\nN7 -> terminal\nN1 -> N8, N7\nN4 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N4, N9assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N4 or N9. Both N4 and N9 lead to terminal nodes, meaning the player who moves to either wins immediately, as the opponent has no legal move. Thus, either move ends the game on the next turn. Since both are terminal moves, either is a winning move. Choosing either results in the same outcome. We select N9 as it appears earlier in the graph and is a valid terminal move.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>", "episode_score": 0.05, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N6, the legal moves are to N4 or N9. Both N4 and N9 lead to terminal nodes, meaning the player who moves to either wins immediately, as the opponent has no legal move. Thus, either move ends the game on the next turn. Since both are terminal moves, either is a winning move. Choosing either results in the same outcome. We select N9 as it appears earlier in the graph and is a valid terminal move.</reason>\n<answer>N9</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N2\n\nDirected graph:\nN3 -> terminal\nN1 -> N9\nN2 -> N4, N1, N6\nN9 -> N0, N7\nN0 -> N4, N7\nN4 -> N8\nN7 -> terminal\nN5 -> terminal\nN6 -> N5, N3\nN8 -> terminal\n\nLegal moves: N4, N1, N6assistant\n", "response": "<reason>Starting at N2, the player can move to N4, N1, or N6. Evaluating each move:  \n- N4 leads to N8 → terminal → immediate win (next player loses).  \n- N1 → N9 → N0 or N7; both eventually lead to terminal via chains, so not optimal.  \n- N6 → N5 or N3; N5 → terminal, N3 → terminal → both lose immediately.  \nBest move: N4 ends the game directly. Therefore, choosing N4 wins immediately. </reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>", "episode_score": -0.6166666666666667, "llm_raw_text": "<reason>Starting at N2, the player can move to N4, N1, or N6. Evaluating each move:  \n- N4 leads to N8 → terminal → immediate win (next player loses).  \n- N1 → N9 → N0 or N7; both eventually lead to terminal via chains, so not optimal.  \n- N6 → N5 or N3; N5 → terminal, N3 → terminal → both lose immediately.  \nBest move: N4 ends the game directly. Therefore, choosing N4 wins immediately. </reason>\n<answer>N4</answer>"}, {"prompt": "system\nYou are playing Directed Acyclic Graph Vertex Geography.user\nThe players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses. Choose one legal destination that maximizes your final game outcome. Keep your thinking process concise.\n\nOutput exactly:\n<reason>your analysis</reason>\n<answer>NODE</answer>\n\nDo not output anything else. A response that does not follow this format results in immediate loss.\n\nCurrent node: N1\n\nDirected graph:\nN7 -> N2\nN2 -> terminal\nN5 -> 